:"","v":[5]},{"id":"kish_1787","name":"Kish","also":"","summary":"The great-grandfather of Mordecai (Esther 2:5).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"shimei_2696","name":"Shimei","also":"","summary":"Son of Gershon.","verses":1,"father":"Kish","mother":"","v":[5]},{"id":"nebuchadnezzar_2167","name":"Nebuchadnezzar","also":"Nebuchadrezzar","summary":"In the Babylonian orthography Nabu-kudur-uzur, which means “Nebo, protect the crown!” or the “frontiers.” In an inscription he styles himself “Nebo’s favourite.”","verses":88,"father":"","mother":"","v":[6]},{"id":"jehoiachin_791","name":"Jehoiachin","also":"Jeconiah, Coniah, Jechonias","summary":"Succeeded his father Jehoiakin (B.C. 599) when only eight years of age, and reigned for one hundred days (2 Chr. 36:9). He is also called Jeconiah (Jer. 24:1; 27:20, etc.), and Coniah (22:24; 37:1).","verses":21,"father":"Jehoiakim","mother":"Nehushta","v":[6]},{"id":"esther_1343","name":"Esther","also":"Hadassah","summary":"The queen of Ahasuerus, and heroine of the book that bears her name. She was a Jewess named Hadas’sah (the myrtle), but when she entered the royal harem she received the name by which she henceforth became known (Esther 2:7).","verses":46,"father":"Abihail","mother":"","v":[7,8,10,11,15,16,17,18,20,22]},{"id":"shaashgaz_2508","name":"Shaashgaz","also":"","summary":"Servant of the beautiful, a chief eunuch in the second house of the harem of king Ahasuerus (Esther 2:14).","verses":1,"father":"","mother":"","v":[14]},{"id":"abihail_32","name":"Abihail","also":"","summary":"The father of Esther and uncle of Mordecai (Esther 2:15).","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[15]},{"id":"bigthana_495","name":"Bigthana","also":"","summary":"One of the eunuchs who “kept the door” in the court of Ahasuerus. With Teresh he conspired against the king’s life.","verses":2,"father":"","mother":"","v":[21]},{"id":"teresh_2842","name":"Teresh","also":"","summary":"Severe, a eunuch or chamberlain in the palace